AppSatbayev Privacy Policy

Last updated 21 November 2026.

Operator and contact

AppSatbayev is an independent student app operated by its developer, @nhslo.
Contact 3578rtuii@gmail.com for access, correction, deletion or questions
about how AppSatbayev handles your data. Keep passwords, session tokens and
academic records out of public issues and support messages.

University account and data on your device

AppSatbayev sends your sign-in credentials directly from your device to
Satbayev University's sign-in service over HTTPS. The developer, Supabase
and our diagnostics service do not receive your university password. If you
explicitly enable Remember Me, the app keeps your login and password in the
device's protected storage until you disable that setting or clear app data.
Session tokens and cookies needed for access are kept in device storage and
cleared on sign-out. Sign-out does not change your Remember Me choice.

The app retrieves the profile, schedule, grades, transcript, journal,
curriculum and course materials you use directly from university services.
It keeps a device cache for offline use and faster loading. For university
responses with a persistent offline cache, typical retention limits are
30 days for standard content, 180 days for academic content and 365 days for
critical records. Some content has a shorter limit or stays in memory.
Preferences, saved credentials and manually saved files are controlled
separately. Sign out to clear the app's university cache or clear the app's
storage in device settings. Files saved outside app storage can be deleted
where you saved them. The university manages the official records.

Optional services

If you enable Microsoft Teams, Microsoft handles sign-in and Microsoft Graph
provides assignments and materials to the app. The app keeps the Teams
session on your device and signs it out when you sign out of the app.

If you enable calendar integration, the app writes the schedule and
reminders you select to a calendar on your device. If that calendar belongs
to a cloud account, its provider synchronizes the events according to the
calendar's settings. Disable synchronization in the app to remove events
created by that integration.

For Android push notifications, Firebase Cloud Messaging provides a device
registration token. The app registers it with the university to deliver
notifications to your device and requests removal when you disable
notifications or sign out. For builds with Sentry crash reporting enabled,
Sentry receives diagnostic information such as crash traces, the app version
and device context to diagnose errors. Provider logs and backups follow the
retention settings of the corresponding service.

Rating with separate consent

In versions that show a separate rating consent screen and connect to the
updated rating service, participation is voluntary. The consent screen
appears when you open the rating. Declining leaves the rest of AppSatbayev
available. Agreement to the Terms of Use does not enroll you.

After you agree, the app sends your university student ID, year of study,
hashed course identifiers, transcript grades and credits, and semester
assessment marks and absence rates to our Supabase rating service. It uses
these data to compute and update the overall and semester rankings. The
server uses your university session token to verify that a request comes
from your account. It forwards that token to the university's protected
profile endpoint and uses the response to verify the student ID. The
rating database does not store the token or the verification response.
Supabase hosts the rating database outside Kazakhstan.

The public leaderboard shows an assigned pseudonym, year of study, position,
GPA and other calculated results. Other users and anyone who accesses the
public rating feed can see those fields. Restricted server records contain
the student ID and the input used to refresh the overall rating. For the
semester rating, the database stores calculated results rather than the
raw journal. You can explicitly enable real-name display in rating settings.
This sends your name to the service and makes it visible on the same public
board. You can switch back to a pseudonym there.

Supabase stores the consent version and time, student ID, rating inputs
and results, and your display preference for participation. A weekly cleanup
removes participant records after 120 days without rating activity. The app
keeps a participation receipt and rating snapshots on the device for
reopening the rating and offline display. The device revalidates older
snapshots when it next fetches a fresh rating.

In Settings > Rating privacy, tap Withdraw consent and delete data. Once
the server confirms the request, your overall and semester entries, pending
results, stored rating inputs and consent record are deleted from the active
service. The app also removes the rating snapshot and receipt for that
account on the current device. Copies previously saved by other viewers and
service backups may persist until those copies expire or are removed.
You can also request deletion by emailing 3578rtuii@gmail.com. This does not
delete the university's records.

Earlier app and server versions

Earlier releases could send rating data when the app loaded the rating for
your account, without the separate opt-in screen. If you still use an earlier
release or cannot access the in-app removal button, email
3578rtuii@gmail.com to request access, correction or deletion of your
existing rating data.
